{"id": "lovesick-melancholy", "ids": "⿸疒愛", "title": "Lovesick Melancholy", "pronunciation": "ài", "bopomofo": "ㄞˋ", "meaning": "A chronic illness of the heart caused by unrequited or impossible love.", "formation": "phono-semantic", "definitions": [{"zh": "因情愛而生之心疾", "en": "An ailment of the heart arising from romantic love"}, {"zh": "思慕成疾，情志不遂之症", "en": "A condition where longing becomes illness, where emotions cannot find their proper course"}, {"zh": "凡深情難捨而致病者", "en": "Any sickness caused by profound affection that cannot be released"}], "etymology": "In the grand pharmacopeia of human suffering, there should have been a character for the particular malady that strikes when love itself becomes pathology. The ancients knew that desire, when thwarted, could manifest as genuine physical illness—what we might call lovesickness transcending mere metaphor. This character would have dignified such affliction with proper medical terminology, acknowledging that the heart's ailments deserve the same gravity as those of any other organ.", "source": {"work": "《集韻》", "gloss": "烏代切，音愛。心疾也。"}, "components": [{"char": "疒", "meaning": "疒"}, {"char": "愛", "meaning": "愛"}], "examples": [{"text": "自君別後，日漸⿸疒愛，藥石無效。", "translation": "Since you departed, I grow daily more lovesick, and no medicine avails.", "style": "classical"}, {"text": "現代人雖不言⿸疒愛，然此症依舊存在於世間。", "translation": "Though modern people don't speak of lovesickness, this condition still exists in the world.", "style": "contemporary"}], "related": [{"char": "癡", "pinyin": "chī", "gloss": "infatuation, obsessive love"}, {"char": "疾", "pinyin": "jí", "gloss": "illness, disease"}, {"char": "憂", "pinyin": "yōu", "gloss": "melancholy, worry"}], "tags": ["emotion", "medicine", "romance", "classical"], "svg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 512 512\" width=\"512\" height=\"512\">\n<style>@import url(\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Noto+Serif+TC:wght@400;700&display=swap\");</style>\n<g transfor